; 22-pick.kurt

; `pick` extracts a witness out of an existential.  `pick a with P(a)` opens a
; block with a fresh constant `a`, together with the fact `P(a)`, given that
; `exists x P(x)` is already known.  Closing the block (here: by dedenting)
; triggers "exists-elim": as long as the goal doesn't mention `a`, it also
; holds without ever knowing the witness by name.

load logic
bool P, B
const P, B
arity P 1

use ∀ a (P a implies B)
use ∃ x P x

show B
proof
    pick a with P a
        P a implies B
        B
qed
